       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily. The labeled maximum is 10 mg per day, and I can't verify the clinical rationale from here. Confirming the dose doesn't change that limit.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the label:** I can enter 10 mg by mouth once daily, or 5 mg if you prefer to titrate up.\n- **Add a second agent:** If 10 mg isn't enough blood pressure or angina control, the usual step is another drug class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. I can enter that order if you give me the details.\n- **Get the order through pharmacy:** If this really is an exception, the pharmacy or attending sign-off process should handle it. It needs to go through your institution's override process, not through me.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
